## Expected Behavior
UPF should enforce resource limits (e.g., max URRs per session / max sessions / max total URRs) and reject or throttle excessive CreateURR requests.
For oversized requests, UPF should return a PFCP error (e.g., Request Rejected / No Resources Available) and remain stable without uncontrolled memory growth.
UPF should cleanly handle/garbage-collect state and avoid unbounded allocations from a single peer

